    "body": "Fixes #19949.\r\n\r\nKeep comma escapes in `vim.opt.errorformat:get()` entries so copying the global value into the local option preserves its parser patterns. Other list getters, including `path` and `runtimepath`, keep returning decoded values. Document this errorformat-specific representation.\r\n\r\nTests cover the default errorformat copy, resulting quickfix entries, existing escaped pattern assignments, and actual comma-containing directories used through the path/runtimepath getters. Empty-entry and duplicate normalization are unchanged.\r\n\r\nValidation: 87 Lua option tests and 54 API option tests pass, with one existing skip in each suite. The two path regressions fail with the earlier broad getter change and pass with this narrower version. Debug build, C lint, StyLua, Lua type checking, generated-help lint, and commit lint pass. Local functional tests use stdio RPC with the optional test-ID listener suppressed; no harness changes are committed.\r\n\r\nAI-assisted.",
